  "notes": "How far a thrown thing carries, and where it comes down when it carries less far than what it was thrown at. A case gives the thing's bulk (null for none), the thrower's strength, the world's gravity (null for none), and the room it was thrown in: its box in its parent's plane (null for a room with no box), the thrower's spot in it, and what the thing was thrown at, a person's spot or a way out's box (null for a way out with no box). range is the bulk's throw_range scaled by ordinary gravity's dice over this gravity's dice (integer division, never under 1) plus (strength - 10) held between 0 and throw_reach_cap, times throw_reach_per_strength; null, and nothing else, with no gravity or a bulk or gravity the tables do not name. distance is the paces along the axes from the thrower to the person, or to the cell of the room beside the doorway it shares with the way out, nearest the thrower, plus one; null, and the range only told, where there is nothing to measure (no box, or a way out with no doorway in this room's walls). short is whether distance is more than range, and landed is the spot range paces along the line towards what it was thrown at, each axis rounded towards the thrower, or null when it was not short. No die is thrown.",
